{"id":"000VU8","title":"Robot Line Lies","author":"raaaaa","solvedCount":6,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-02T17:09:21+00:00","posted":"Heute, 10:20 Uhr","rules":"I recently discovered marty_sears's Liar Cell series and really enjoyed it. It also reminded me of Robot Lines, a constraint I had only seen used in two puzzles. I decided to try combining the two ideas to create a new sudoku, and this puzzle is the result.\n\nClick the image to play the puzzle.\n\nRules:\n\nPlace the digits 1-9 once in each row, column and 3x3 box of the main grid.\n\nLIAR CELLS: Exactly one cell in every row, column and 3x3 box is a liar. A liar has two different numbers: the DIGIT written in the grid and the real VALUE used by the other clues. For every other cell, digit and value are equal.\n\n• The nine liar digits are the numbers 1-9, with no repeats.\n\n• The nine liar values are also the numbers 1-9, with no repeats.\n\nROBOT LINES: Each blue-grey line has an inspection robot, with its initial stop marked by a red circle. From any inspected cell, its real VALUE gives the exact number of cell-to-cell steps to the next stop. The robot chooses one direction for that move, then may choose either direction again after stopping. It cannot turn around midway through a move or travel beyond an open end. On a closed loop, it continues around the loop as needed.\n\nThe inspection ends only after every cell on that robot's line has been visited as a stop exactly once; the final cell's value imposes no further move. A move may pass through earlier stops, but may not end on one. Each robot stays on its own line.\n\nX / V: The real values of two cells separated by an X add to 10; those separated by a V add to 5.\n\nBLACK DOTS: The two real values joined by a black dot have a 1:2 ratio.\n\nWHITE DOTS: The two real values joined by a white dot differ by 1.\n\nNot every qualifying X, V, black dot or white dot is marked.\n\nNOTES: In the blue arrow beside a row, you may note the digit in that row's liar cell. Use the grey-blue circle beside it for the corresponding real value. These notes are optional.","solutionCode":"For each row, enter the real VALUE of its liar cell, from top to bottom (9 digits, no spaces)","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/q0z1ef0wl6","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/q0z1ef0wl6","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":12,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-02T17:09:21+00:00"}